WEBVTT

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:03.510
A clean shot from the prince's blade!

00:00:03.510 --> 00:00:04.390
<i>Got you!</i>

00:00:07.810 --> 00:00:09.730
<i>He bent his elbow...</i>

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:12.400
<i>...to alter the angle of the punch!?</i>

00:00:14.830 --> 00:00:16.910
A right turns his jaw upward!

00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:18.400
A left!

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:19.910
Right!

00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:22.250
A left-right combo!

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:24.620
The challenger is being hammered!

00:00:27.890 --> 00:00:29.880
It's another down!

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:31.420
The challenger's second down!

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:34.380
The champion's hidden strength erupts!

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:37.210
<i>Damn it...</i>

00:00:37.210 --> 00:00:40.030
<i>for him to go after my counter like this.</i>

00:00:40.030 --> 00:00:42.650
<i>I've never been this pissed before.</i>

00:00:42.650 --> 00:00:45.390
<i>It feels like he just ripped the pride out of my chest.</i>

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:49.530
<i>I won't lose like this!  {changed to be consistant with Ep 2 TL Check}</i>

00:00:55.690 --> 00:00:58.830
The challenger faces his second down in this round!

00:00:58.830 --> 00:01:00.870
The damage is serious!

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:02.770
His face is stained crimson!

00:01:02.770 --> 00:01:05.710
Will he be able to keep fighting!?

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:09.990
<i>Damn it all.</i>

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:12.680
<i>My counter...</i>

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:15.470
<i>My pride, you're making a mockery of it.</i>

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:17.440
Get up, Miyata!

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:19.180
Don't let it end here!

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:21.970
We didn't come here to see you like this!

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:24.470
Miyata-kun!

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:27.230
Ichiro!

00:01:27.570 --> 00:01:31.970
Miyata's counter was sharper than I anticipated.

00:01:31.970 --> 00:01:36.890
That's why it managed to land in the first round while we were still laying out the bait.

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:40.460
But it won't work anymore!

00:01:40.460 --> 00:01:42.670
We let you study it on purpose!

00:01:42.670 --> 00:01:45.410
Even if you do stand up, there's nothing you can do!

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:52.630
<i>I am not... going to lose like this!</i>

00:01:55.110 --> 00:01:56.120
He's up!

00:01:58.560 --> 00:01:59.870
I'm good to go, Referee.

00:02:00.650 --> 00:02:01.640
Move aside.

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:09.720
Even if you stand up, your counter is blocked off!

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:12.510
A boxer without a way of finishing off their opponent is nothing to worry about!

00:02:12.510 --> 00:02:15.280
You're like a bird with a broken wing!

00:02:17.810 --> 00:02:19.530
It looks like the damage is significant!

00:02:19.810 --> 00:02:22.030
The challenger isn't steady on his feet!

00:02:22.470 --> 00:02:25.540
If he falls again, the fight will officially be over!

00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:27.110
There are 20 seconds left!

00:02:27.110 --> 00:02:29.280
Can the challenger survive this pinch!?

00:02:30.020 --> 00:02:31.220
A right!

00:02:31.220 --> 00:02:32.540
It's barely blocked!

00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:34.010
Run, Miyata!

00:02:34.010 --> 00:02:35.730
Use a clinch to buy some time!

00:02:36.190 --> 00:02:37.710
<i>I won't let him clinch.</i>

00:02:37.710 --> 00:02:38.920
<i>I'll keep pushing him with punches.</i>

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:43.720
Whoa, the challenger fights back!

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:45.810
<i>He's really got some guts.</i>

00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:49.100
Left-right combos!

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:51.270
The challenger is pushed to the ropes in an instant!

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:53.620
Don't get stuck on the ropes!

00:02:52.690 --> 00:02:54.770
Get away and try to stall!

00:02:53.620 --> 00:02:54.770
Run!

00:02:56.930 --> 00:02:57.930
He doesn't back down!

00:02:57.930 --> 00:02:59.280
He fights back!

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:02.280
Why are you fighting it out!?

00:03:00.890 --> 00:03:02.280
You need to make it to the third round!

00:03:02.790 --> 00:03:04.280
He's hit again!

00:03:04.460 --> 00:03:08.490
His face is twisted and his legs buckle, but he doesn't fall!

00:03:09.210 --> 00:03:11.010
He just keeps fighting back!

00:03:11.010 --> 00:03:12.120
Ten seconds left!

00:03:12.350 --> 00:03:14.650
Please run!

00:03:13.460 --> 00:03:14.650
Don't fall!

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:16.620
The champion is on the warpath!

00:03:17.410 --> 00:03:18.630
But he still fights back!

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:22.130
Whoa, the challenger's legs shake! He can't hide his damage!

00:03:22.670 --> 00:03:24.140
The champion's right!

00:03:25.490 --> 00:03:26.380
<i>I can counter this one!</i>

00:03:27.070 --> 00:03:28.560
The counter failed!

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:30.430
The challenger's face is knocked backwards!

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:32.440
Five seconds left!

00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:35.310
He fires back!

00:03:35.310 --> 00:03:36.480
Only three seconds!

00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:38.860
Two seconds!

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:40.110
One second!

00:03:42.490 --> 00:03:44.120
H-He...

00:03:44.360 --> 00:03:45.410
He falls!

00:03:46.290 --> 00:03:48.880
That's the third down!

00:03:49.710 --> 00:03:52.780
<i>M-Miyata-kun...</i>

00:03:52.780 --> 00:03:53.860
<i>lost?</i>

00:03:58.100 --> 00:03:59.380
Slip!

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:01.940
It's declared a slip!

00:04:01.940 --> 00:04:03.560
Not a down!

00:04:03.560 --> 00:04:07.390
The entire audience held its breath for a moment!

00:04:08.310 --> 00:04:11.640
The bell has rung! The second round is over!

00:04:13.990 --> 00:04:16.070
My heart stopped...

00:04:16.780 --> 00:04:18.900
And it looks like he got the life sucked out of him.

00:04:19.370 --> 00:04:21.270
That was dangerous.

00:04:21.270 --> 00:04:23.510
Why did he get so pissed off?

00:04:23.510 --> 00:04:26.390
It seemed too aggressive and too reckless.

00:04:26.390 --> 00:04:29.410
Was Miyata's boxing always this rough?

00:04:29.780 --> 00:04:31.010
It had to be rage.

00:04:31.810 --> 00:04:32.890
Rage?

00:04:32.890 --> 00:04:35.540
Miyata has never really been all that durable.

00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:38.580
It wouldn't have been odd if he'd lost from that second down.

00:04:39.260 --> 00:04:42.960
But after having his counter preyed on and his pride wounded...

00:04:43.550 --> 00:04:46.170
it was rage that kept Miyata standing.

00:04:47.610 --> 00:04:48.680
<i>That's right... {jama: added}</i>

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:51.930
<i>I have a counter that I can finish people off with.</i>

00:04:52.770 --> 00:04:55.050
<i>Even without relying on brute force,</i>

00:04:55.050 --> 00:04:57.440
<i>I can KO anyone.</i>

00:04:57.760 --> 00:05:01.570
<i>Counters are the embodiment of Miyata-kun's pride itself.</i>

00:05:01.570 --> 00:05:03.280
But now what!?

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:05.890
With his counters blocked off, he doesn't have any decisive punches.

00:05:05.890 --> 00:05:07.200
It's gonna be tough!

00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:09.910
The real question is, how will the next round turn out?

00:05:09.910 --> 00:05:12.460
Whether he goes on the offensive or tries to defend,

00:05:12.460 --> 00:05:16.680
it hinges on how much stamina he can get back and how much damage he can recover from before the next round.

00:05:18.610 --> 00:05:21.210
<i>I hate to say it, but he won't recover.</i>

00:05:21.210 --> 00:05:23.900
<i>Miyata's weight control is harder than most people can imagine.</i>

00:05:23.900 --> 00:05:27.340
<i>After being hit that much and fighting back so hard,</i>

00:05:27.340 --> 00:05:29.970
<i>he's gotta be almost out of gas.</i>

00:05:30.470 --> 00:05:32.720
<i>I don't want to admit it, but this match...</i>

00:05:35.510 --> 00:05:36.730
We've won.

00:05:37.120 --> 00:05:40.340
To think he'd be able to fight back in that condition...

00:05:41.250 --> 00:05:44.990
That must be the fabled 
"Japanese Spirit" you hear so much about.

00:05:45.630 --> 00:05:50.580
But he doesn't seem to realize how badly his body is crippled because of his weight management.

00:05:50.580 --> 00:05:54.200
They're the actions of a fool who doesn't think ahead!

00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:58.510
At this rate, Miyata's nothing more than a moving sandbag-

00:05:57.190 --> 00:05:58.510
Stop it,

00:05:58.510 --> 00:05:59.750
Mr. Sakaguchi.

00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:04.690
I've never seen a boxer this brave before.

00:06:05.380 --> 00:06:07.720
Without a doubt, he is the greatest challenger.

00:06:07.720 --> 00:06:09.720
Arnie...

00:06:10.320 --> 00:06:13.980
I am going to show Miyata my respect by KO'ing him with all my strength.

00:06:13.980 --> 00:06:16.020
You just shut up and watch.

00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:20.860
Otherwise, this will be the last time you use me as your cash cow.

00:06:24.340 --> 00:06:26.310
This is really bad.

00:06:26.310 --> 00:06:28.740
I got pissed and fought back,

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:31.530
but now I can't even dodge punches that I'm able to see coming.

00:06:31.530 --> 00:06:34.060
I'm starting to resent this fragile body.

00:06:34.060 --> 00:06:35.410
Stop talking.

00:06:35.410 --> 00:06:37.540
Be quiet and try to save your strength.

00:06:38.980 --> 00:06:40.940
<i>What do I do?</i>

00:06:40.940 --> 00:06:44.190
<i>I hate to admit it, but his strategy against counters is almost perfect.</i>

00:06:44.190 --> 00:06:46.890
<i>My trademark speed is shot...</i>

00:06:46.890 --> 00:06:51.290
<i>If I remain cautious from here on out, I'd only be prolonging things.</i>

00:06:52.510 --> 00:06:56.150
<i>Even if it's suicidal, I have to keep fighting back.</i>

00:06:56.150 --> 00:06:59.860
<i>I'll pour all my remaining stamina into it and keep punching!</i>

00:06:59.860 --> 00:07:01.770
<i>If I keep it up, I might luck out.</i>

00:07:02.780 --> 00:07:05.570
So you intend to keep him on edge and hope you land a lucky punch?

00:07:07.340 --> 00:07:12.310
I'm sure you don't realize what kind of situation you are in.

00:07:12.310 --> 00:07:16.440
They call you clever, but in reality you're more stubborn than anyone else.

00:07:16.440 --> 00:07:20.410
Rather than suffer a shameful decision, you'll choose to risk it all for an honorable defeat.

00:07:20.410 --> 00:07:23.080
I realized something recently.

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:27.040
After decades of being involved with boxing, it's become clear to me...

00:07:27.040 --> 00:07:30.300
Although I would have never admitted it while I was still a fighter...

00:07:30.690 --> 00:07:33.010
In boxing, there is no such thing as a lucky punch!

00:07:34.500 --> 00:07:38.680
When I retired, I complained that I was hit with a so-called "lucky punch."

00:07:38.680 --> 00:07:40.970
But I was wrong.

00:07:40.970 --> 00:07:45.520
A punch that's thrown by someone who's given up on the match will never land.

00:07:45.520 --> 00:07:49.190
And even if it does, you can't knock someone out with a dead fist.

00:07:50.600 --> 00:07:54.200
Now, as someone who's moved on to training fighters, I've figured it out.

00:07:55.410 --> 00:07:59.490
Some do it for fame and glory, some do it for money.

00:07:59.490 --> 00:08:02.710
There are many reasons, but they all withstand brutal training.

00:08:03.130 --> 00:08:05.870
They hit the sandbag tens of thousands of times,

00:08:05.870 --> 00:08:09.530
and put all of their feelings into their fists.

00:08:09.530 --> 00:08:12.070
It may seem like a punch landed as a fluke,

00:08:12.070 --> 00:08:15.220
but that's a punch that has been thrown tens of thousands of times.

00:08:15.780 --> 00:08:18.140
It's a living fist!

00:08:20.220 --> 00:08:22.780
Never, ever giving up until the end...

00:08:22.780 --> 00:08:26.480
Those living fists are what give birth to miracles!

00:08:30.860 --> 00:08:34.820
<i>Now that he mentions it, I guess I've seen that sort of thing before.</i>

00:08:35.670 --> 00:08:37.170
<i>I'll do it.</i>

00:08:37.650 --> 00:08:38.990
<i>No,</i>

00:08:38.990 --> 00:08:40.990
<i>I have a reason that I have to do it.</i>

00:08:41.340 --> 00:08:42.830
Seconds out!

00:08:46.820 --> 00:08:48.750
Thank you, Dad.

00:08:50.340 --> 00:08:51.980
Now, just watch...

00:08:53.300 --> 00:08:56.590
and see if my fists are still alive.

00:08:57.640 --> 00:08:59.420
Round 3!

00:09:01.250 --> 00:09:03.820
The challenger survives the desperation of the second round,

00:09:03.820 --> 00:09:06.270
but he's definitely weakened now.

00:09:06.270 --> 00:09:08.730
Will the champion be able to finish him off in this round?

00:09:09.330 --> 00:09:12.230
Who will the Oriental Pacific Region Belt end up with?

00:09:12.780 --> 00:09:14.020
Now...

00:09:14.720 --> 00:09:15.740
Wait...

00:09:16.120 --> 00:09:17.420
they don't move!

00:09:17.420 --> 00:09:19.360
They're staring each other down in the ring!

00:09:19.360 --> 00:09:21.240
This is an awfully quiet start to the round!

00:09:21.600 --> 00:09:25.110
The champion doesn't intend to let him rest.

00:09:25.110 --> 00:09:28.320
The fact that he's being careful here shows that he's gotten used to fighting him.

00:09:28.320 --> 00:09:32.500
If he's still not showing any openings at this point, a comeback KO is gonna be tough.

00:09:34.460 --> 00:09:35.560
<i>Miyata-kun...</i>

00:09:36.100 --> 00:09:39.230
<i>After being damaged so badly and having your counter blocked off,</i>

00:09:39.810 --> 00:09:41.010
<i>what will you do?</i>

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:44.110
Now, who will move first?

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:45.520
<i>He's coming.</i>

00:09:47.870 --> 00:09:48.900
One-two!

00:09:49.610 --> 00:09:50.970
It's sharp! And fast!

00:09:50.970 --> 00:09:52.900
The champion's expression changes!

00:09:53.530 --> 00:09:54.900
<i>It tore through the air.</i>

00:09:55.470 --> 00:09:57.900
<i>He's still saving a punch worth being cautious for.</i>

00:09:59.300 --> 00:10:00.570
Now he presses inward!

00:10:00.570 --> 00:10:03.960
The challenger seems like he wants to fight it out!

00:10:03.960 --> 00:10:05.560
Has he recovered from the damage?

00:10:05.560 --> 00:10:06.320
Get him!

00:10:06.320 --> 00:10:08.080
Take him down!

00:10:08.710 --> 00:10:10.280
<i>It's not surprising.</i>

00:10:10.280 --> 00:10:12.480
<i>I anticipated this attack.</i>

00:10:12.480 --> 00:10:14.670
<i>This is the choice that someone as brave as him would make.</i>

00:10:15.510 --> 00:10:18.480
<i>Fighting hard and losing, it's a suicide strategy.</i>

00:10:19.470 --> 00:10:21.300
A right and a left!

00:10:21.300 --> 00:10:23.430
The champion is caught!

00:10:25.580 --> 00:10:26.180
<i>Wha-  {jama:added}</i>

00:10:26.930 --> 00:10:28.810
<i>What's that look in his eyes?</i>

00:10:29.490 --> 00:10:31.310
<i>He doesn't think this is suicide!</i>

00:10:31.640 --> 00:10:33.860
<i>He's clearly still trying to win!</i>

00:10:34.050 --> 00:10:35.080
<i>Fight back!</i>

00:10:35.080 --> 00:10:37.360
<i>If I don't fight back, his spirit's going to overwhelm me!</i>

00:10:38.140 --> 00:10:41.500
The champion fires back as if drawn in by the challenger's fighting spirit!

00:10:41.500 --> 00:10:42.750
They're really going at it!

00:10:42.750 --> 00:10:45.120
Expertly thrown punches go flying!

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:48.640
Who will come out on top in this test of strength!?

00:10:48.640 --> 00:10:50.050
The champion!?

00:10:50.050 --> 00:10:51.870
Or the challenger!?

00:10:55.250 --> 00:10:58.000
<i>Dammit, I saw that punch coming!</i>

00:10:58.000 --> 00:11:00.130
<i>I saw it, but I couldn't dodge it!</i>

00:11:00.990 --> 00:11:03.020
<i>My reflexes are sluggish.</i>

00:11:03.020 --> 00:11:04.890
<i>I have to keep my nerves on edge.</i>

00:11:04.890 --> 00:11:06.720
<i>Focus! Focus!</i>

00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:10.190
Beautiful!

00:11:10.190 --> 00:11:12.400
A triple left, like lightning!

00:11:12.600 --> 00:11:14.560
What are you wasting time for!?

00:11:14.560 --> 00:11:16.830
Your opponent's groggy!

00:11:16.830 --> 00:11:18.480
Hurry and finish him already!

00:11:19.240 --> 00:11:21.410
<i>The end of your days as my cash cow?</i>

00:11:21.410 --> 00:11:24.120
<i>You're part of my stable.</i>

00:11:24.120 --> 00:11:28.790
<i>I'm going to make sure I make money off of you even after you fight in a world title match.</i>

00:11:29.370 --> 00:11:31.340
Has the challenger found his rhythm!?

00:11:31.340 --> 00:11:32.870
The champion is trapped against the ropes!

00:11:32.870 --> 00:11:34.830
Has he recovered from the damage!?

00:11:35.250 --> 00:11:36.490
<i>He's still hurt,</i>

00:11:37.030 --> 00:11:39.550
<i>but his remarkable mental strength is letting him overcome it.</i>

00:11:40.120 --> 00:11:43.970
<i>I can't change the flow here unless I remind him how badly he's hurting.</i>

00:11:44.470 --> 00:11:45.050
<i>A body blow!</i>

00:11:45.680 --> 00:11:47.040
<i>His guard is tight!</i>

00:11:47.550 --> 00:11:49.060
<i>But he will fight back!</i>

00:11:49.540 --> 00:11:52.060
<i>And when he does, I'll really lay into him!</i>

00:11:55.290 --> 00:11:56.060
<i>Here it comes!</i>

00:11:56.720 --> 00:11:58.020
<i>Now, time it with a right!</i>

00:12:01.160 --> 00:12:03.800
He goes for the counter, but pulls his hand back!

00:12:03.800 --> 00:12:06.080
<i>I can't! He's aiming for my counters!</i>

00:12:06.290 --> 00:12:07.630
<i>You hesitated.</i>

00:12:10.500 --> 00:12:11.620
A body blow!

00:12:11.620 --> 00:12:13.830
It sinks in deep!

00:12:25.530 --> 00:12:26.800
<i>Now time it with a right!</i>

00:12:30.010 --> 00:12:32.630
He goes for the counter, but pulls his hand back!

00:12:32.630 --> 00:12:34.850
<i>I can't! He's aiming for my counters!</i>

00:12:35.130 --> 00:12:36.570
<i>You hesitated.</i>

00:12:39.270 --> 00:12:40.470
A body blow!

00:12:40.470 --> 00:12:42.610
It sinks in deep!

00:12:45.550 --> 00:12:46.450
Ichiro!

00:12:46.930 --> 00:12:48.620
The challenger is stopped in his tracks!

00:12:48.620 --> 00:12:50.450
The champion pours it on!

00:12:50.950 --> 00:12:54.410
A single hit was all it took to turn it around!

00:12:54.410 --> 00:12:57.210
Was he that hurt all along?

00:12:57.530 --> 00:12:58.980
<i>You've done well,</i>

00:12:58.980 --> 00:13:02.590
<i>but at this point your mind can't deny the damage to your body.</i>

00:13:02.880 --> 00:13:05.590
<i>Now, I just have to sever your consciousness to put an end to your fighting spirit.</i>

00:13:05.590 --> 00:13:07.680
<i>I just have to throw this last punch!</i>

00:13:10.750 --> 00:13:12.600
<i>It's over, Miyata.</i>

00:13:16.330 --> 00:13:18.100
<i>Impossible! He's fighting back?</i>

00:13:21.900 --> 00:13:23.230
<i>What is this?</i>

00:13:23.230 --> 00:13:24.190
<i>How...</i>

00:13:24.600 --> 00:13:26.740
<i>can he still fight back when he's hurt this much?</i>

00:13:29.560 --> 00:13:31.190
<i>You can't just write this off as fighting spirit.</i>

00:13:31.190 --> 00:13:34.370
<i>Something else is supporting Miyata right now.</i>

00:13:34.660 --> 00:13:36.370
<i>What in the world could...?</i>

00:13:37.710 --> 00:13:40.380
<i>I made a promise.</i>

00:13:47.750 --> 00:13:48.890
<i>Miyata-kun...</i>

00:13:49.650 --> 00:13:51.350
<i>This time,</i>

00:13:51.350 --> 00:13:53.390
<i>I'll make it a reality.</i>

00:13:57.790 --> 00:14:01.900
<i>I can't let it... remain unfulfilled.</i>

00:14:05.870 --> 00:14:10.410
<i>I can't leave the ring as a liar again!</i>

00:14:11.780 --> 00:14:12.910
Miyata-kun!

00:14:13.290 --> 00:14:15.390
You can do it, Miyata!

00:14:14.070 --> 00:14:15.390
Miyata-kun!

00:14:15.390 --> 00:14:16.800
Don't give up!

00:14:16.800 --> 00:14:18.660
The champion's hesitating!

00:14:28.150 --> 00:14:29.330
<i>Stop worrying.</i>

00:14:29.330 --> 00:14:31.250
<i>This doesn't change the fact that I'll win.</i>

00:14:31.250 --> 00:14:35.180
<i>I should hurry and put his restless soul at ease.</i>

00:14:35.680 --> 00:14:37.560
<i>With the next attack, I'll stop him for good!</i>

00:14:39.800 --> 00:14:41.170
The champion moves forward!

00:14:41.170 --> 00:14:43.560
A big step that indicates a heavy left!

00:14:46.570 --> 00:14:47.430
Stop!

00:14:47.430 --> 00:14:48.670
There's the bell!

00:14:48.670 --> 00:14:51.070
Just as the fighters' fists crossed, the bell rings!

00:14:51.540 --> 00:14:54.080
The third round is over!

00:14:57.310 --> 00:14:58.950
You're wasting time!

00:14:58.950 --> 00:15:01.210
You've had plenty of chances to finish him already!

00:15:01.490 --> 00:15:02.780
I understand.

00:15:02.780 --> 00:15:04.890
You were letting Miyata intimidate you!

00:15:04.890 --> 00:15:06.360
What an embarrassment!

00:15:06.360 --> 00:15:08.590
Can't you consider my position as the person who set this match up!?

00:15:08.990 --> 00:15:13.020
If you can't finish someone off in a situation like this, your value as a fighter is going to start dropping!

00:15:14.590 --> 00:15:15.850
More business talk?

00:15:16.700 --> 00:15:17.960
Of course!

00:15:17.960 --> 00:15:19.900
You're a pro!

00:15:19.900 --> 00:15:22.090
It's your job to attract a big crowd!

00:15:22.090 --> 00:15:23.830
Relax.

00:15:23.830 --> 00:15:25.260
I'll finish him in the next round.

00:15:25.260 --> 00:15:26.920
Oh, I see!

00:15:26.920 --> 00:15:28.580
Now that's what I wanted to hear!

00:15:28.580 --> 00:15:30.110
Good, good.

00:15:31.770 --> 00:15:34.620
Before you get excited, you might want to think about what you're going to do with yourself next.

00:15:36.650 --> 00:15:39.590
As a manager, you earned your keep.

00:15:39.590 --> 00:15:42.150
And I was taking advantage of that, but...

00:15:42.670 --> 00:15:47.120
I don't feel like returning to a corner that doesn't consider its boxer's feelings anymore.

00:15:47.120 --> 00:15:49.130
W-What do you mean by that?

00:15:49.680 --> 00:15:51.580
Mr. Sakaguchi...

00:15:51.580 --> 00:15:52.880
You're dismissed.

00:15:54.040 --> 00:15:55.690
This is the end of our partnership.

00:15:57.660 --> 00:16:00.690
You think I'll let you get away with that?

00:16:00.690 --> 00:16:02.890
I've got a signed contract, you know!

00:16:03.330 --> 00:16:05.770
I do want to thank you for one thing.

00:16:05.770 --> 00:16:08.820
Somehow you, who doesn't think of boxing as anything other than business,

00:16:08.820 --> 00:16:11.940
managed to find me the greatest challenger imaginable at the very end.

00:16:11.940 --> 00:16:14.590
In the end? You must be kidding!

00:16:14.590 --> 00:16:16.370
This whole time, it's been give-and-take-

00:16:16.370 --> 00:16:17.350
Get lost.

00:16:18.850 --> 00:16:21.190
After I beat Ichiro Miyata...

00:16:21.900 --> 00:16:24.170
I'll go for the world title myself.

00:16:24.830 --> 00:16:26.050
Wa...

00:16:26.050 --> 00:16:27.500
Water...

00:16:27.500 --> 00:16:29.170
Don't gulp it down.

00:16:33.380 --> 00:16:35.240
<i>That hits the spot.</i>

00:16:35.860 --> 00:16:39.540
<i>I don't know how much it'll matter with me out of gas, but...</i>

00:16:40.090 --> 00:16:43.220
<i>One punch... Now, I have at least enough for one more punch.</i>

00:16:43.820 --> 00:16:46.150
<i>That's all I need.</i>

00:16:47.240 --> 00:16:51.650
<i>If it's a counter with all my weight behind it, one punch will be all I need.</i>

00:16:52.860 --> 00:16:54.400
Seconds out!

00:16:55.750 --> 00:16:56.770
Ichiro!

00:17:01.130 --> 00:17:02.410
Get it done!

00:17:06.920 --> 00:17:09.410
<i>He looks ready.</i>

00:17:09.410 --> 00:17:12.100
<i>He intends to end it in this round.</i>

00:17:12.100 --> 00:17:14.670
<i>He must realize he's already at his limit.</i>

00:17:15.090 --> 00:17:16.750
Round 4!

00:17:17.420 --> 00:17:18.340
Box!

00:17:19.670 --> 00:17:21.430
<i>You're out there watching, right?</i>

00:17:21.670 --> 00:17:24.430
<i>I haven't forgotten that promise I made with you.</i>

00:17:25.720 --> 00:17:26.940
<i>I will fulfill it!</i>

00:17:27.670 --> 00:17:28.530
Whoa!

00:17:29.200 --> 00:17:30.460
He's waving him in!

00:17:30.460 --> 00:17:34.280
The challenger is boldly telling the champion to bring it on!

00:17:34.280 --> 00:17:36.850
How will the champion answer!?

00:17:36.850 --> 00:17:38.520
<i>Impressive.</i>

00:17:38.520 --> 00:17:40.290
<i>There's no way I can run from this.</i>

00:17:40.290 --> 00:17:42.530
<i>I'll take you head on!</i>

00:17:43.460 --> 00:17:45.270
It's a straight up fight!

00:17:45.270 --> 00:17:46.450
Left! Right!

00:17:46.450 --> 00:17:48.170
Sharp punches slice through the air!

00:17:48.800 --> 00:17:52.420
<i>If I kept my distance and fought, it would be easy to wrap this up.</i>

00:17:53.040 --> 00:17:56.670
<i>But how could I call myself the champion if I backed down from a half-dead boxer?</i>

00:17:57.310 --> 00:18:00.250
<i>I don't want to protect the Pacific Region Belt by being defensive.</i>

00:18:00.250 --> 00:18:02.680
<i>I want to go on the offensive and take the world title!</i>

00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:04.180
<i>This is a sharp offensive.</i>

00:18:04.180 --> 00:18:06.310
<i>But I'm grateful for it.</i>

00:18:06.310 --> 00:18:09.150
<i>To think he'd accommodate me when he knows how badly I'm hurt.</i>

00:18:09.730 --> 00:18:12.150
He doesn't let himself get overwhelmed! He fights back with combinations!

00:18:12.480 --> 00:18:13.620
<i>Not enough!</i>

00:18:13.620 --> 00:18:15.400
<i>Your punches are already dead!</i>

00:18:15.650 --> 00:18:18.120
Whoa, the challenger is struck!

00:18:18.120 --> 00:18:19.320
He's pushed back to the ropes!

00:18:19.580 --> 00:18:20.340
No good!

00:18:20.340 --> 00:18:21.980
He can't fight back in that condition!

00:18:21.980 --> 00:18:23.830
Don't overdo it! Try to clinch!

00:18:24.200 --> 00:18:26.000
He's hoping to land one more.

00:18:26.000 --> 00:18:27.730
Dammit, Miyata!

00:18:27.730 --> 00:18:28.730
A counter?

00:18:28.730 --> 00:18:30.580
But the Bloody Cross is still...

00:18:31.670 --> 00:18:33.940
<i>He's overwhelmed by power.</i>

00:18:33.940 --> 00:18:36.200
<i>There's only one punch that can change the outcome.</i>

00:18:36.200 --> 00:18:37.290
<i>The counter!</i>

00:18:38.370 --> 00:18:40.080
<i>He doesn't have enough stamina to make any mistakes.</i>

00:18:40.580 --> 00:18:42.840
<i>It might be suicide, but he has to use it!</i>

00:18:43.910 --> 00:18:46.170
<i>Either way, this...</i>

00:18:47.060 --> 00:18:48.600
<i>will be the last one.</i>

00:18:49.130 --> 00:18:51.360
The champion fires away in spite of the guard!

00:18:51.360 --> 00:18:53.360
Is it only a matter of time until it gets split open!?

00:18:53.850 --> 00:18:56.280
<i>You've got no hope at close range either.</i>

00:18:56.280 --> 00:18:57.820
<i>I'm going to finish this!</i>

00:18:58.890 --> 00:19:01.360
A liver blow penetrates deep!

00:19:01.690 --> 00:19:04.710
A single attack that might be enough to cripple the challenger!

00:19:05.210 --> 00:19:07.120
<i>Is this it?</i>

00:19:09.350 --> 00:19:11.870
A right is aimed downward at his sinking jaw!

00:19:12.460 --> 00:19:14.460
Was that the decisive blow!?

00:19:15.850 --> 00:19:17.460
<i>No, not yet.</i>

00:19:18.610 --> 00:19:20.360
<i>I still haven't thrown it yet.</i>

00:19:21.110 --> 00:19:24.120
<i>This single shot of energy deep inside me...</i>

00:19:24.660 --> 00:19:26.390
<i>I haven't used it yet!</i>

00:19:26.800 --> 00:19:28.100
<i>It's over!</i>

00:19:31.230 --> 00:19:32.140
<i>This is it!</i>

00:19:35.500 --> 00:19:37.080
<i>He's stepping into the punch!</i>

00:19:37.080 --> 00:19:37.900
<i>A counter!?</i>

00:19:38.120 --> 00:19:40.380
<i>This is the last bit of strength I have saved...</i>

00:19:40.380 --> 00:19:42.410
<i>with everything I have behind it!</i>

00:19:42.630 --> 00:19:44.660
<i>Go!</i>

00:19:48.040 --> 00:19:49.160
It was stopped!

00:19:49.160 --> 00:19:51.090
Here comes the Bloody Cross!

00:19:51.090 --> 00:19:52.790
No! He can't dodge it!

00:19:53.220 --> 00:19:55.040
<i>Is it all over!?</i>

00:19:55.250 --> 00:19:58.030
<i>As soon as I push this hand aside, it's the end!</i>

00:19:58.030 --> 00:19:59.040
<i>Goodbye,</i>

00:19:59.040 --> 00:20:00.300
<i>Ichiro Miyata!</i>

00:20:10.850 --> 00:20:12.060
<i>He's pushing it back!?</i>

00:20:13.140 --> 00:20:14.320
<i>It's not just his arm strength.</i>

00:20:14.980 --> 00:20:16.940
<i>His entire body... is behind it!</i>

00:20:32.600 --> 00:20:33.200
He's... {jama: sub this?}

00:20:33.880 --> 00:20:36.200
He's down!
